Z||000006||Cheever2||11-07-2000||01:37 PM||||The interview went great!!! They need people, and they're willing to train.  They just want somebody who knows something about PBX's as opposed to knowing nothing.  So the experience I had may be enough to get my foot in the door.  Didn't have to fill out any papers, and he didn't ask stupid HR questions.  Nothing he described about the job changed my mind about wanting it, and he seemed satisfied with me.  Now I have to wait.  I might hear something in a few weeks, or maybe not until near the end of the year.  But I came out of the meeting feeling like I will probably get the job.  Yea!!!  <BR>Thanks for the well-wishing.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Cheever2||01-09-2001||07:34 PM||||<B>GOOD NEWS!!!!!!!</B> (that's 7 exclamation marks)<BR>Although Southwestern Bell is <I>still</I> dragging their feet, I got another job almost just like it!  <B>Yea!</B><BR>Going to start in two weeks at Williams Communications, doing PBX & T-1 tech work via remote site.  Best of all, it's dayshift Monday thru Friday.  After almost 25 years, I'm finally getting out of mainframe computer operations.  Man, this feels good.  Think I'll take the family out someplace nice to dinner (my other family, not all <I>you</I> guys).  That big whooshing sound you hear is my sigh of relief.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
